.TH INSERT 1 "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "@PROJECT_AUTHOR@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
insert \- insert text or file contents into a file at a line position
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B insert
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIFILE\fR [\fISRC\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B insert
splices the contents of each
.I SRC
into the target
.I FILE
at a chosen line position.
The target is rewritten only when the result differs
(atomic write via a temporary file beside the target).
.PP
By default each
.I SRC
is an
.B extended
source (\fB\-e\fR):
if it begins with
.BR @ ,
the remainder is a filename to read;
otherwise the argument is a string literal.
.PP
When no position option is given,
.B insert
appends to the end of the file.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Source modes
These options are mutually exclusive; the last one wins.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-strings
Treat each
.I SRC
as a string literal (raw bytes, plus any trailing newlines from
.BR \-\-blank ).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-filenames
Treat each
.I SRC
as a path to read.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-extended
Extended sources (default):
.BI @ FILE
reads from
.IR FILE ;
any other argument is a string literal.
.SS Position
.TP
.BI \-n " NUM"
Insert before 1-based line
.IR NUM .
If the file has fewer than
.I NUM
lines, empty lines are appended after the end of the file
(and a missing final newline is added first if needed)
so the inserted content lands on line
.IR NUM .
.TP
.BR \-0 " .. " \-9
Digit short options that accumulate into a decimal number
(for example
.B \-20
is
.B 2
then
.BR 0 ).
.RS
.TP
.B \-1
Same as
.BR \-\-prepend .
.TP
.B \-0
Prepend the content and then one blank line
(content appears before the original start, separated by an empty line).
.TP
.B \-N
(with
.IR N " \(>= 2)"
Same as
.BI \-n " N"
(insert before line
.IR N ,
with end-of-file padding when necessary).
.TP
After
.B \-a
Digits select append style:
.B 0
appends at end;
.B 1
or greater inserts before the Nth line from the end.
.RE
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-append
Append-oriented position.
.B \-a
or
.B \-a0
appends at the end of the file (like shell
.BR >> ).
.B \-a1
inserts before the last line;
.BI \-a N
(with
.IR N " \(>= 1)"
inserts before the
.IR N th
line from the end.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prepend
Prepend to the start of the file.
.TP
.BI \-r " NUM" "\fR, \fB\-\-remove=" NUM
Remove
.I NUM
lines at the insert point before inserting.
With no
.I SRC
arguments this deletes those lines.
Examples:
.RS
.TP
.B insert \-3 \-r2 FILE
Delete lines 3 and 4.
.TP
.B insert \-p \-r1 script.sh \[aq]#!/bin/whale\[aq]
Replace the shebang.
.TP
.B insert \-a1 \-r1 FILE newfoot
Replace the last line (footer).
.RE
When
.B \-r
is used with no insert content and the line position is past the end of the file,
no empty lines are padded; only deletion is attempted (often a no-op at EOF).
When no
.I SRC
is given at prepend (\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-1\fR, \fB\-0\fR),
.I NUM
specifies how many lines to remove from the beginning (1-based).
With \fB\-0\fR, the count is relative to the blank line (e.g. \fBinsert \-0 \-r3 FILE\fR on \fIa/b/c/d/e\fR yields \fIc/d/e\fR).
With \fB\-1\fR, the count is exact (e.g. \fBinsert \-1 \-r3 FILE\fR on \fIa/b/c/d/e\fR yields \fId/e\fR).
.SS Source formatting
.TP
.BI \-b " NUM" "\fR, \fB\-\-blank=" NUM
Append
.I NUM
newline characters after each
.IR SRC .
When this option is omitted, the default is
.B 1
for string literals and
.B 0
for filenames
(under
.BR \-e :
string arguments vs
.BI @ FILE ).
When
.B \-b
is given, the same
.I NUM
applies to every
.IR SRC .
.TP
.BI \-m " TEXT" "\fR, \fB\-\-missing=" TEXT
If a filename source cannot be read, use
.I TEXT
instead of failing.
Missing-text is treated like a string for
.B \-\-blank
defaults.
.SS Common
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase logging verbosity (may be repeated).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Decrease logging verbosity.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, missing target, I/O failure, or out of memory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Prepend a header line (string default adds a trailing newline):
.PP
.nf
insert \-p notes.txt Header
.fi
.PP
Insert a file snippet before line 20 (pads if the file is shorter):
.PP
.nf
insert \-20 notes.txt @snippet.txt
.fi
.PP
Delete lines 3–4:
.PP
.nf
insert \-3 \-r2 notes.txt
.fi
.PP
Replace the shebang:
.PP
.nf
insert \-p \-r1 script.sh \[aq]#!/bin/whale\[aq]
.fi
.PP
Replace the footer line:
.PP
.nf
insert \-a1 \-r1 notes.txt newfoot
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LANGUAGE
.TQ
.B LC_ALL
.TQ
.B LC_MESSAGES
.TQ
.B LANG
Select the language for messages and translated man pages when available.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @PROJECT_AUTHOR@.
